1
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,850
Don't worry, Alexandra.

2
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:07,900
We'll find the owner.

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,640
How, Robbie?

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:11,500
Let me think.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,670
Gemma, sit.

6
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:13,900
Good Gemma.

7
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,030
Give me your paw.

8
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:16,380
Good Gemma.

9
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:17,970
This dog is well trained.

10
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:19,620
She likes you, too.

11
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,790
So how are we going to find the owners?

12
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:25,150
With a little help from the ASPCA,

13
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,740
the American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals.

14
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:29,950
They're the ones.

15
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:31,570
We once found a cat.

16
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:33,530
She was caught in the branches of our tree.

17
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:35,540
And Dad called the ASPCA.

18
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:37,100
They came and solved the problem.

19
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:43,270
Robbie, let's call them.

20
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:50,840
Let me see -- ASPCA...

21
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:51,420
Here it is.

22
00:00:51,420 --> 00:01:01,960
ASPCA Animal Shelter.

23
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:12,500
555-7700.

24
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:14,610
Hello, ASPCA.

25
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:17,460
Hello, my name is Robbie Stewart.

26
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,820
I have a lost dog I'd like to bring to you.

27
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:21,050
How late are you open?

28
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:22,970
We're open till nine P.M.

29
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:23,510
Thank you.

30
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:25,160
I'll bring the dog over by nine.

31
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:25,840
Thanks.

32
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:27,230
Bye.

33
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:27,640
Thanks.

34
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:36,420
Good-bye.

35
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:37,940
They're still open?

36
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:38,970
They're open until nine o'clock.

37
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:41,080
We have two and a half hours.

38
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:42,370
Let's take Gemma by there now.

39
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:44,940
They'll find the owner.

40
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:46,540
I hope so.

41
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:49,920
I'm so sad to see this little dog without her family.

42
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,560
I'm sure they'll find the owner.

43
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:55,430
But if they don't, I'll adopt her.

44
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:59,280
She's so cute.

45
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:02,220
Look at those eyes.

46
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,670
She's hard to resist.

47
00:02:03,670 --> 00:02:07,280
Don't you just love her?

48
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,360
I'd like to keep her, too.

49
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,930
But I'll be going home to Greece

50
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:13,540
at the end of the semester.

51
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:19,330
She just wants love and affection.

52
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:20,000
Come on, Robbie.

53
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,650
Let's get her to the animal shelter,

54
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:24,810
so they can find her owners quickly.

55
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:25,990
Don't worry, Gemma.

56
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:27,770
We'll get you home.

57
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:30,200
It's not easy being away from home.

58
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,610
Come on, poochie.

59
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:34,260
Atta girl!

60
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,520
Let's go.

61
00:02:35,520 --> 00:03:00,970
We're off to the animal shelter.

62
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:01,940
Your name?

63
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,410
Robbie Stewart.

64
00:03:03,410 --> 00:03:05,830
And this is Alexandra Pappas.

65
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:10,730
Your name will do, Mr. Stewart.

66
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:14,770
Your address?

67
00:03:14,770 --> 00:03:18,800
46 Linden street, Riverdale.

68
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,460
Where did you find the dog?

69
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:22,040
She found us.

70
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:24,090
You tried calling the number on the collar?

71
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:27,540
Yes, but the number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,780
And there's no address on the dog tag?

73
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:32,170
There's no other information.

74
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,920
No ID number.

75
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:37,670
Without that, it's hard.

76
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:40,110
You will try to find the dog's owner.

77
00:03:40,110 --> 00:03:43,310
Oh, we'll try, believe me.

78
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:45,270
And if you don't?

79
00:03:45,270 --> 00:03:47,160
Yes?

80
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:50,900
If you don't ... can I ... can I adopt the dog?

81
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,080
Why, yes.

82
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,780
If the owners don't claim the dog in forty-eight hours,

83
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:56,800
then you can apply for adoption.

84
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:57,990
How do I do that?

85
00:03:57,990 --> 00:03:59,490
You really want to?

86
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:01,320
Yes, I'm serious.

87
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:03,040
If no one comes to claim Gemma,

88
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,990
I'd like to adopt her.

89
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:07,990
It's not difficult.
